Z||000000||Monkeyman||12-10-1999||03:12 AM||||Anybody tell me how to unzip a file?  I just downloaded PIP (it made it to "MY Documents").  The destructions say to unzip it, but I can't figure out how to do that.  I can't even open it.  I get a window that says it's not a valid Win32 file (whatever that means).  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierospeeder||12-10-1999||03:26 AM||||is it a *.zip file?<BR>go to <A HREF="http://www.winzip.com" TARGET=_blank>www.winzip.com</A>  if it is and download a trial verson of winzip 7<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||12-10-1999||04:32 AM||||Yes, you need a program like WinZip. It'll also only run on Win9x or Win2000.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-10-1999||05:03 AM||||I'm running Win98 and I have WnZip already.  How do I use it?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Scott2M4||12-10-1999||07:40 AM||||Fire up WinZip and select <B>Open Archive...</B> from the <B>File</B> pull-down menu.  From the next window, make sure you're in the directory that contains the PIP zip file, select it and hit the <B>Open</B> button.  You should then see a window with a list of files.  Choose the <B>Select All</B> option from the <B>Actions</B> pull-down menu then choose the <B>Extract...</B> option from the same pull-down menu.  WinZip will ask you where you wish to dump the files.  Select a directory, hit the <B>Extract</B> button and you're finished unzipping.  From there, follow the instructions Cliff has on the site.<P>BTW, I'm running Windows NT SP4 and PIP seems to work great on it.<p>[This message has been edited by Scott2M4 (edited 12-10-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||William Federle||12-10-1999||08:19 AM||||What sort of pgm is PIP||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||12-10-1999||11:23 AM||||<B>P</B>ennock's <B>I</B>mage <B>P</B>oster is a program that makes posting pics on the forum quick and easy.  Plus, they are stored on cliffs machine so we wouldnt have to worry with the problems stemming from loading a pic from another machine on the net. <P>Go to the announcements section and pull up posts from last couple of months and look for topic "beta testers wanted"||||reg||1
